  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It passes `typecheck`, but I could not run `vite build` or load the page in a browser. The physics, rendering and label placement are therefore untested.\n\n- **Scene:** The board is 8 wide and 12 tall, with a back panel, side walls, a top bar and a faint transparent front pane. It has 8 staggered peg rows alternating 7 and 6 pegs, and 7 bins separated by dividers. Pegs, balls and bins use different materials. A key light and a blue rim light light the scene, with a neutral environment for fill. The camera is a fixed perspective view of the whole board.\n- **Physics:** I wrote my own 2D circle physics instead of using the engine's Rapier physics, to keep it deterministic. It runs at a fixed 1/120 s step with gravity, restitution 0.4, and collisions with pegs, walls, dividers, the floor and other balls.\n- **Stuck-ball nudge:** A ball that lands exactly on a peg or divider top would balance there forever. For example, ball 4 has a zero offset and lands on the centre peg. A deterministic nudge pushes any such ball sideways after 0.3 s.\n- **Spawning:** \"Drop 20 Balls\" spawns one ball every 0.25 simulated seconds from the top centre, using the specified offset formula. The 20 ball nodes are created up front and moved each frame. \"Reset\" clears all balls and counts.\n- **Labels and buttons:** The buttons, bin numbers 1 to 7 and live counts are DOM elements over the canvas. I placed them by projecting the camera with a 40° vertical field of view. If the engine's projection differs, the labels will sit slightly off their bins.\n- **State and ready flag:**\n  - `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only getter returning `{phase, spawned, bins, total}`, updated every frame.\n  - A bin counts a ball once its centre is below the divider tops.\n  - The phase becomes `settled` after all 20 balls have spawned and are at rest in bins.\n  - `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the frame after the first draw.",
